  "section_path_text": "Another Thanksgiving Rally?",
  "level": 0,
  "ordinal": 0,
  "summary": "On this day last year, the tanker market was on the brink of one of the most dramatic rate spikes of all time - although no one saw it coming. On the Wednesday before the traditional Thanksgiving holiday in the United States, VLCC rates were Worldscale 85 and ships were earning about $44,000 per day. What a difference a day makes as rates spiked 50 points on Thursday leading to the strongest 12 month period for tanker rates in recent history.",
